      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — clearer variable names, proper AAA structure, and meaningful comments.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version improves understandability by renaming `handler` to `triggeredDeprecatedOptions` (making its purpose self-evident), replacing the cryptic `opt1`/`opt2`/`opt3` names with descriptive ones (`simpleDeprecatedOption`, `richDeprecatedOption`, `regularOption`), removing the `@formatter:off/on` directives in favor of natural line breaks, and organizing the test into clear Arrange/Act/Assert sections with a brief Javadoc explaining the overall intent."
